{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"FIRST LIVE RUN ON NATIVE AMD64 — THE HARNESS WORKS. GitHub Actions run 30507727332, job 'jira DC harness smoke', on merged commit a20ccd89b.\nSTEP-BY-STEP, this is the vindication of the whole build-not-pull + amd64 diagnosis:\n  Build and start the Jira DC harness .......... SUCCESS\n  Wait for Jira DC to become ready ............. SUCCESS\n  Run the Jira DC harness smoke tests .......... failure (3 passed, 1 error)\n  Tear down .................................... SUCCESS\nThe instance BUILT from the vendored Dockerfile, BOOTED, and ANSWERED REST — in about 7 minutes wall-clock for the whole job, against three local attempts that never got there in 25-55 minutes. Native amd64 was exactly the missing ingredient, and Cargo's 600000ms ceiling never fired.\nWHAT THE 3 PASSING TESTS PROVE (these are the substantive ones):\n * test_instance_is_a_server_deployment_at_the_pinned_version — it really is Jira 8.x with deploymentType != Cloud, so DC's REST v2 semantics are what we are exercising, not Cloud's v3+ADF.\n * test_personal_access_token_authenticates_via_bearer — PAT BEARER AUTH WORKS against a real 8.17.1, minted programmatically via POST /rest/pat/latest/tokens. That is the DC auth mode J6's transport will use, now proven rather than assumed.\n * test_a_bogus_bearer_token_is_rejected — the contrast case, so the PAT result is not an artifact of the endpoint accepting anything.\nTHE ONE FAILURE was MY fixture, not the harness: it hardcoded projectTemplateKey 'com.pyxis.greenhopper.jira:gh-simplified-kanban-classic' — a plausible, widely-cited Software template — and the instance replied '400 The project template specified does not exist'.\nFIX (change 1019): I did NOT substitute another guess. That would be the third time in this story I guessed an identifier and was wrong (pullable image name; -DstartupTimeout/-Dcargo.timeout). The instance is the only authority on which templates it has, so the fixture now DISCOVERS them via GET /rest/project-templates/latest/templates and tries each in turn, then a bare software project, then a bare project, taking the first 201. On total failure it reports EVERY attempt with its status instead of a lone 400, so a future image bump says what it tried.\nALSO CAUGHT DURING THE EDIT: my insertion left the original '@pytest.fixture' decorator attached to the new _discover_project_templates helper, which would have made a plain helper into a fixture and broken it when called directly. Found by checking decorator placement with an AST walk after the edit rather than trusting that a clean 'ruff check' and a successful collect meant the structure was right — neither would have caught it.\nJ5 remains IN_PROGRESS. Its ACs require the smoke tests to actually pass; 3 of 4 is not done."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785377984548288001,"uuid":"9822fcb6-166a-4a04-9c76-a424b8a87bb0"}